1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:05,213
You can't search for something you don't know exists.
That's why I built UnseenPath.

2
00:00:09,100 --> 00:00:18,628
UnseenPath starts by learning a student's grade, experience with the U.S. school system,
interests, and goals, so every recommendation begins with context.

3
00:00:21,350 --> 00:00:32,017
Instead of waiting for students to know the right question, UnseenPath proactively introduces
important school concepts, upcoming preparation, and resources they may not know about.

4
00:00:32,300 --> 00:00:40,545
Students can explore academic fields and career paths, from technology and health
to art, business, engineering, and public service.

5
00:00:40,900 --> 00:00:51,599
Opportunities include competitions, programs, research, and projects. Each one explains why
it may be useful, and verified resources link to official information.

6
00:00:56,200 --> 00:01:02,005
Career Explorer helps students compare many directions
without treating any one path as a permanent decision.

7
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:13,003
When something matters, students can save it, set a goal, and move it
from planned, to in progress, to completed.

8
00:01:17,300 --> 00:01:23,786
UnseenPath turns discovery into understanding, planning, and action.
Discover what you didn't know to ask.
